output:
  narrator:
    word: narrator
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: The person who tells a story, or the voice through which a story is told, whether first-person,
      omniscient, or unreliable. In a documentary, the narrator is the voice-over guiding the viewer through the
      footage.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun
    origin: feed
  plan:
    word: plan
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: A set of intended steps toward a goal, or a drawing that lays out a building or machine from above
      in simplified, symbolic form. As a verb, to design something or to work out how to achieve it. In enough's
      MacroCOSM OES, what a compiled program will do, set out as an ordered graph of its steps that can be inspected
      before anything runs.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun; verb
    origin: feed
  delay:
    word: delay
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: A period of time before something happens, or the act of putting something off; as a verb, to postpone
      or hinder. In audio, a delay is an effect that repeats a sound after a short interval.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun; verb
    origin: feed
  ask:
    word: ask
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To put a question to someone, or to request something from them. It can also mean to require or
      expect something, as a task or situation does.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb
    origin: feed
  goal:
    word: goal
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: Something a person aims to achieve, or in sports, the area or act of sending the ball or puck into
      it, and the point scored for doing so.
    pos_primary: noun
    pos: noun; verb
    origin: feed
  protect:
    word: protect
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To keep someone or something safe from harm, danger, or damage.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb
    origin: feed
  sits:
    word: sit
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: 'To rest with the body''s weight on the buttocks rather than standing, or to move into that position.
      Loosely, it can mean to occupy a place, hold a session, or simply remain: a house may sit empty, a jury may
      sit for weeks.'
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  has:
    word: have
    frequency_rank: 7
    definition: To possess, hold, or experience something, or to include it as a feature; to cause something to
      be done; or, with "to," to be obliged; and serves as an auxiliary forming perfect tenses. As a noun, a have
      is a wealthy or privileged person.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  kept:
    word: keep
    frequency_rank: 6
    definition: To hold onto, retain, or continue to have; to maintain in a given condition or place; to observe
      or fulfil, as a promise or a rule; to look after or provide for. As a noun, the fortified tower at the heart
      of a castle; the food and money needed to support someone.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  stands:
    word: stand
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To support oneself upright on the feet, or to remain in place without moving; as a noun, a position
      taken, a piece of furniture that holds things upright, or a spot where something is sold or performed. Taking
      a stand means holding firm on a matter despite opposition.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  says:
    word: say
    frequency_rank: 6
    definition: To speak words aloud; to state or assert; of a text, sign, or instrument, to convey information.
      As a noun, the right or chance to influence a decision; as an adverb, approximately or for example.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun; adverb; interjection
    origin: feed
  holds:
    word: hold
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To grasp, contain, or keep possession of something, from a hand holding a cup to a shelf holding
      books. As a noun it can be a grip, a place where animals or prisoners are kept, or a ship's cargo space below
      deck.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  feeds:
    word: feed
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To give food to someone or an animal, or to eat; as a noun, food given to non-human animals, or
      any material supplied continuously into a system.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  follows:
    word: follow
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To go or come after a person or thing; to pursue; to happen or come next in sequence; to obey or
      act in accordance with; to understand the sense of, as in following an argument.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; noun
    origin: feed
  those:
    word: that
    frequency_rank: 7
    definition: Indicating a person or thing more distant, already mentioned, or understood from context, as determiner
      or pronoun; also the conjunction introducing a subordinate clause, as in she said that she would come.
    pos_primary: determiner
    pos: determiner; pronoun; conjunction
    origin: feed
  asks:
    word: ask
    frequency_rank: 5
    definition: To put a question to someone, or to request something from them. It can also mean to require or
      expect something, as a task or situation does.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb
    origin: feed
  assumed:
    word: assumed
    frequency_rank: 4
    definition: Adopted, especially a name or identity, in order to deceive or conceal; also, more broadly, supposed
      to be true without being checked.
    pos_primary: verb
    pos: verb; adjective
    origin: feed
